WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.438 --> 00:00:03.480
(upbeat music)

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:06.060
- [Narrator] This may look
like just another car factory,

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:08.340
but it's actually a new microfactory,

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.380
manned by autonomous robot dogs

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:12.873
and robotic arms monitored by AI.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.400
It's designed to change
the way cars are produced,

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.650
and it's been built in the
heart of one of the smallest

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:22.563
and most expensive countries
in the world, Singapore.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:26.970
Typically, car manufacturers
don't build car factories

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:29.310
in dense urban cities like Singapore,

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:31.800
but here it's gonna be different
for most car factories.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.310
Robots are going to do a
lot of the manufacturing

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:38.490
and it's gonna be a much
more flexible model.

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:41.010
- [Narrator] Microfactories
reinvent the way cars are made

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:42.990
by automating most of the process

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:44.550
and building them in a cell

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:46.920
rather than along a production line.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:49.350
- This could be the
future in which we talk

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:51.210
in a couple of years from now.

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:53.160
- [Narrator] Microfactories
are one of the biggest changes

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:56.700
to car making in a generation
and if the concept is proven,

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:58.800
it could shape the future of the industry.

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:02.550
For over a hundred years,

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:04.290
cars have been built in large plants,

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:06.420
manned by hundreds of workers.

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:09.630
The trend has been towards
building bigger factories.

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:13.307
Tesla's Gigafactory facility
located near Austin, Texas,

00:01:13.307 --> 00:01:15.420
covers more than 10 million square feet

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:17.970
of factory floor space,
and has the capacity

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:21.330
to build more than
250,000 vehicles a year.

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:23.610
By comparison, Hyundai's, new Microfactory

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:27.210
in Singapore stands just
over 935,000 square feet.

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:29.010
The car makers to the plant could produce

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:31.470
up to 30,000 cars a year.

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:34.260
Hyundai has pushed aside the
traditional assembly process

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:36.750
to allow for a much smaller footprint.

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:39.360
- Behind me, there are robots
that are putting together

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:41.730
the final finishing touches on a car.

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:44.640
Typically, in a more conventional
manufacturing process

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:47.130
that would actually
largely be done by humans,

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:49.500
it would be done in a long assembly line

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:52.155
which doesn't allow
for much customization.

00:01:52.155 --> 00:01:52.988
(bright music)

00:01:52.988 --> 00:01:54.210
- [Narrator] In
traditional auto factories,

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:56.310
vehicles travel along a linear path

00:01:56.310 --> 00:01:59.220
and parts are installed
along an assembly line.

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:01.530
While the procedure is
increasingly automated,

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:04.860
the basic process hasn't
significantly changed.

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:06.180
- Here it's different.

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:08.070
It's a cell-based model, which means

00:02:08.070 --> 00:02:10.920
that there are different
cells around the factory floor

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:13.170
where they're are focused
on different tasks,

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:16.620
and that actually allows
for a lot more automation.

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:18.390
- [Narrator] In each
cell, robots are tasked

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:19.920
with installing several components

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:23.370
of the car before it's
moved to the next zone.

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:25.800
Cells can be modified with
different instructions,

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:28.440
from installing parts in
an identical car design,

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:30.873
to assembling a different
vehicle altogether.

00:02:31.770 --> 00:02:35.100
Hyundai says that more than 50%
of the manufacturing process

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:38.310
at its Singapore microfactory
is done by robots.

00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:41.463
Automated ground vehicles move
the cars around the factory,

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:46.410
while four-legged robots
equipped with AI cameras monitor

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:48.210
and analyze the assembly.

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:50.460
Issues identified by the robot dogs

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:52.350
are then fixed by human workers.

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:53.700
- Even though we're a small factory,

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:56.070
we're producing cars
as a mass manufacturer.

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:59.970
So what allows us to do that is the usage

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:04.650
of flexible automation and a large portion

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:07.320
of systems intelligence behind

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.720
to orchestrate the manufacturing.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:10.553
- [Narrator] Hyundai says,

00:03:10.553 --> 00:03:12.450
because production is highly automated,

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:14.430
only about a hundred
workers would be needed

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:17.760
to produce the plant's capacity
of 30,000 cars per year.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:20.280
That means a worker at the
microfactory could produce two

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:21.930
to three times the number of cars

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:24.900
compared to a person in
a traditional factory.

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:28.200
- For sure, we will still
need large scale factories.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:30.090
We will still need to produce as many cars

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:32.310
as possible the most effective way

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:35.280
when it comes to overall mobility.

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:37.530
But we feel that the
answer is not only that,

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:41.550
and that in an urban environment,
having a smaller factory

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:44.580
that allows us to produce
as many different types

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:47.460
of mobility devices in
a cost-effective way

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:48.960
is absolutely critical.

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:50.370
- Hyundai's plant in Singapore

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:54.120
is the country's first auto
factory in over 40 years.

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:56.460
While microfactories could
allow wealthier countries

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:58.560
to rebuild manufacturing industries,

00:03:58.560 --> 00:03:59.940
the move toward greater automation

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:02.160
will mean fewer manual jobs for workers.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:05.130
- In a typical assembly
plant, you would think

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:08.190
for the assembly operation
of high single digit

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:10.590
to double digit percentage of automation

00:04:10.590 --> 00:04:14.340
of automated tasks, we
are at around 50% already.

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:19.170
When it comes to logistics,
the provision at the right time

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:22.110
of the right part to the right cell

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:26.130
is again something where we've
automated over 60% already.

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:29.640
It's also in very low double
digit in other factories,

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:30.903
it's essentially manual.

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:34.470
- [Narrator] Microfactories
are largely untested ground

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:35.970
for the auto industry.

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:39.210
Arrival, an EV startup
producing vans has committed

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:42.150
to manufacturing their
vehicles out of microfactories.

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:44.790
However, the company has
only delivered a small number

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:48.180
of the vehicles that forecasted
out of its plant in the UK.

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:50.820
Arrival has struggled
to ramp up production

00:04:50.820 --> 00:04:54.900
and a push back a plan second
microfactory in the US.

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:57.690
For now, Hyundai says it's
the only major car maker

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:00.150
to start building vehicles out of one.

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:02.730
- We have a thesis for
the future of mobility.

00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:06.300
As we test the market, if we
realize that this is right,

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:09.570
you could see smart urban mobility hubs

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:11.700
in many different urban environments.

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:13.590
- [Narrator] While the
concept behind microfactories

00:05:13.590 --> 00:05:15.660
remains unproven at a mass scale,

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:18.150
they provide a glimpse into
what car making could look like

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:19.830
as the industry heads towards a future

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:21.331
that is more automated.

00:05:21.331 --> 00:05:23.914
(gentle music)

